From: Crane's Lab (local fix archive)
Subject: mt76x0u: add vnd_reset module parameter to skip firmware vendor reset

Some MT7610U hardware revisions become permanently unresponsive after
the vendor reset performed in mt76x0u_load_firmware(): the ASIC/MAC
revision reads succeed, then every subsequent vendor request times
out (-110) and rx URBs stall (-32) until the probe gives up.

Gate the reset behind a new bool module parameter "vnd_reset".
Default is 0 (skip the reset), which makes the affected devices
probe cleanly; vnd_reset=1 restores the upstream behaviour.

Verified on a white-label AC600 adapter (USB 0e8d:2870 -> 0e8d:7610,
ASIC revision 76100002, MAC revision 76502000) running OpenWrt
24.10.8 / kernel 6.6.144, mt76 snapshot eb567bc7: with the stock
driver the probe fails after ~50 s of -110/-32 errors; with this
patch the probe completes in ~2 s, an ieee80211 phy appears, and
dual-band scan works (2.4 GHz: 19 BSSs, 5 GHz: 3 BSSs).

Same failure and workaround as documented for an AVM 057c:8502
adapter (identical ASIC/MAC revisions) in
https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/issues/454

---
--- a/mt76x0/usb_mcu.c
+++ b/mt76x0/usb_mcu.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/firmware.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/moduleparam.h>
 
 #include "mt76x0.h"
 #include "mcu.h"
@@ -13,6 +14,19 @@
 #define MCU_FW_URB_MAX_PAYLOAD		0x38f8
 #define MCU_FW_URB_SIZE			(MCU_FW_URB_MAX_PAYLOAD + 12)
 
+/*
+ * Some MT7610U devices become unresponsive after the firmware
+ * vendor reset in mt76x0u_load_firmware(): subsequent vendor
+ * requests time out (-110) and rx URBs stall (-32), so the probe
+ * never finishes. Gate the reset behind a module parameter.
+ * See https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/issues/454
+ * Default is to skip the reset.
+ */
+static bool vnd_reset;
+module_param(vnd_reset, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(vnd_reset,
+		 "Perform vendor reset during firmware upload (default: 0)");
+
 static int
 mt76x0u_upload_firmware(struct mt76x02_dev *dev,
 			const struct mt76x02_fw_header *hdr)
@@ -127,7 +141,8 @@
 	mt76_set(dev, MT_USB_DMA_CFG,
 		 (MT_USB_DMA_CFG_RX_BULK_EN | MT_USB_DMA_CFG_TX_BULK_EN) |
 		 FIELD_PREP(MT_USB_DMA_CFG_RX_BULK_AGG_TOUT, 0x20));
-	mt76x02u_mcu_fw_reset(dev);
+	if (vnd_reset)
+		mt76x02u_mcu_fw_reset(dev);
 	usleep_range(5000, 6000);
 
 	mt76_wr(dev, MT_FCE_PSE_CTRL, 1);
